# JXP + RevEngine API development

This API is built on [JXP](https://github.com/WorkSpaceMan/jxp). Framework changes belong in the **jxp** repo; app-specific models, hooks, and business logic belong in **revengine-api**.

## Repositories

| Repo | Path (local) | Role |
|------|----------------|------|
| **revengine-api** | workspace root | RevEngine models, `bin/server.js`, segment/report logic |
| **jxp** | `../jxp` (sibling clone) | Framework: REST layer, auth, schema base, query/populate |

Open **`revengine-jxp.code-workspace`** (parent `Development/` folder) in Cursor to load both roots in one session.

## Local jxp (live framework edits)

```bash
# One-time: clone next to this repo
git clone https://github.com/WorkSpaceMan/jxp.git ../jxp
cd ../jxp && npm install --legacy-peer-deps

# In revengine-api: use local jxp (creates .use-local-jxp; survives npm install)
npm run link:jxp

# Back to published npm package
npm run unlink:jxp
```

`link:jxp` also symlinks `mongoose` (and `mongoose-friendly`) from this app into `../jxp/node_modules` so both use one connection. Without that, linked jxp loads its own mongoose and queries like `apikeys.findOne()` buffer until timeout.

After changing jxp or re-running `link:jxp`, restart the API (`npm run dev`). Run jxp tests from `../jxp`: `npm test`.

## Version note

- **npm** (`jxp` ^2.15): currently 2.x (e.g. 2.16).
- **GitHub master** (`../jxp`): 3.x — breaking changes possible when linked.

When linked to master, treat compatibility fixes as part of the jxp 3 upgrade. Prefer fixing framework behavior in jxp when the bug is generic; keep RevEngine-only rules in this repo.

## Where to change what

| Change | Repository |
|--------|------------|
| New field type, populate, permissions, generic hooks | `jxp/libs/`, `jxp/models/` |
| RevEngine models (`reader`, `segment`, …) | `revengine-api/models/` |
| API-wide hooks / Mongo connection | `revengine-api/bin/server.js` |
| Deep import e.g. `jxp/libs/query_manipulation` | Framework API — consider exporting from jxp `package.json` `exports` if stabilizing |

